Paseo Relay is the relay server for Paseo, the agentic development
environment (misc/paseo).  It forwards traffic between a Paseo daemon and
its remote clients, such as the Paseo mobile app, so that the daemon needs
no open inbound port: the daemon connects out to the relay and clients
meet it there.  Traffic is end-to-end encrypted between the daemon and each
client, so the relay sees only addresses, timing, message sizes, and
session IDs.

This is the relay that runs relay.paseo.sh, for people who want to run
their own.
